Unknown option: --bogus
bbapprove v1.0.0-rc.2 — approve and merge Renovate PRs on Bitbucket Server.

Usage: bbapprove [--apply] [--hide-ignored] [--disallow a,b] [--token-name NAME]
                 [--config FILE] [--print-config] [-i] [--no-mouse] [PR_URL...]
       bbapprove --init [--force] [--config FILE]
       bbapprove doctor [--offline] [--config FILE]
       bbapprove --outdated [--pre]
       bbapprove --update [--yes] [--pre]

Dry run by default: with no PR_URL every open PR where you are a reviewer is listed and only
eligibility is reported. Nothing changes without --apply.

Options:
  --apply            approve, then merge, the eligible PRs
  --hide-ignored     leave ignored PRs out of the table
  --disallow a,b     also skip PRs whose title mentions these dependencies
  --token-name NAME  1Password item that holds the API token
  --config FILE      use this config file
  --print-config     show the effective settings and where each came from (no secrets)
  --init             create the config file from the template (--force replaces one)
  -i                 interactive TUI (--no-mouse turns mouse capture off)
  --outdated         check whether a newer release exists (--pre includes pre-releases)
  --update           update after showing a plan (--yes skips the question)
  -V, --version      print the version
  -h, --help         this help
  doctor             diagnose the installation and the configuration

Topics: bbapprove help TOPIC
  rules   which PRs are eligible, the ignore list, the STATUS column
  tui     the interactive TUI: columns, status bar, exit summary, mouse
  config  config file lookup, precedence, first run, --init, --print-config
  token   where the API token comes from
  update  --outdated and --update
  env     environment variables and exit codes
  doctor  bbapprove doctor, the diagnostics report
